// Chapter 6: Grand reopening, in English. [draft] Translated by Claude Code from chapter6.ink; it follows that file
// line for line (same knots, lines, speakers and choice ids; the parity test in Story/Tests checks it). Change the
// dialect file first, then this one. [[word]] marks a tap-to-explain word; its English meaning is in the Glossary table.

EXTERNAL chose(knot)

// [draft]
=== rooftop_stairs ===
Yazan, the [[oud]] can wait. Boxes first, then you can sing. #karim
But listen to these stairs, boss… every step has its own note. #yazan #smile
Yazan strums as he climbs, and the sound climbs with him. #sys
The wood on these stairs is old, but it has a strong heart. Like the [[Hajjeh]], God rest her. #karim
Yazan, you play on the pavement every day. On opening night, the roof is yours. #salma #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== rooftop_lights ===
Oh… you can see all of Amman from here. The hills are nothing but lights. #salma #surprised
What is this view? It's like the houses are tumbling down from the sky. #lana #surprised
[[Teta]] came up to the roof every sunset. She said she was saying hello to the neighbourhood. #salma
Now I know why. #salma #smile
Fine, but don't cry before we've hung the lights. #lana #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== new_sign ===
In Dubai we'd hold a whole meeting for one name… okay, I forgot I'm back. #salma #smile
I want a name people in Riyadh know too. #lana #thinking
The whole street says “[[Gahwit Sitti]]”. And wood doesn't learn a new name at its age. #karim
“Sitti”, “my grandmother”? She's my grandmother too, you know. #lana
And when you say it, she's yours. So the name belongs to both of us. #salma #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== invitations ===
You've written an invitation for every house on the street… who's the last one for? #lana
For Mom. #salma #sad
“Mom, the opening is next Thursday. The seat behind the counter is still yours.” #salma
I sent my mother a photo of the invitation. She didn't reply… but she saw it. #lana #sad
Maybe that's how things start… with a look. #salma
-> END

// [draft]
=== flowers ===
Armfuls of white roses arrive, with sprigs of basil tucked between them. There's no card. #sys
No name? Who sends flowers and doesn't sign them? #lana #surprised
Mom. No one but her puts basil in a bouquet. #salma #surprised
She used to say: the roses are for the eyes, and the basil is for your Teta. #salma #sad
She didn't come… but her scent did. That's a step, my girl. #abu_fadi
-> END

// [draft]
=== opening_night ===
The café is full to the brim, and so is the roof. People are even sitting on the stairs. #sys
{
- chose("menu_board") == "saudi":
    Saudi coffee comes first on the board… and Abu Fadi ordered nothing but the Ammani. Never mind, he'll get used to it. #lana #smile
- else:
    See? Ammani coffee comes first on the board… and everyone's ordering the Saudi. What did I tell you? #lana #smile
}
I was the first customer here, in '74. I never thought I'd see it this full again. #abu_fadi
Im Khalil used to say: a café isn't walls, it's people. And you… you are the people. #abu_fadi #smile
Salma keeps glancing at the door. The seat behind the counter is still empty. #sys
-> END

// [draft]
=== m6_lead ===
This roof has seen a wedding before tonight. My mother's, in '74. #samira
Your mother's wedding? But you were already around in '74! #salma #surprised
My father, God rest him, died when I was little. That year my mother married again… and your Teta sewed her dress. #samira
-> END

// [draft]
=== m6_intro ===
Im Khalil, people will talk. A widow, wearing white? #samira_mother_1974
Let them talk. A bride is a bride, the first time or the second. #teta_young
And you, Samira, hold the pins tight, and don't swallow a single one. #teta_young #smile
The line is drawn in chalk. The needle follows it; it never runs ahead. #teta_young
-> END

// [draft]
=== m6_perfect ===
Not one stitch off the line. That's how you sew a dress for a lifetime. #teta_young #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== m6_ok ===
A crooked stitch here and there… no one will see it. The groom will only see the bride. #teta_young #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== m6_outro ===
By God, Im Khalil… I never thought I'd wear white again. #samira_mother_1974
My dear, a heart has more than one door. And tonight the whole street dances on the roof. #teta_young #smile
That night, little Samira danced until she fell asleep in Teta's lap. And the sewing box went back on its shelf. #sys
-> END

// [draft]
=== m6_return ===
To this day my mother says: “Im Khalil sewed me a dress, and sewed my luck in with it.” #samira #smile
Now then, whose turn is it? I have a groom all ready… #samira
No, [[Khalto]] Samira. Keep the grooms in their box. #lana #smile
-> END
